92186573270 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186573173 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573270 #edb/ref 1069 "q-131369" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573270 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573270 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573270 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "402decfa-8c35-5ba9-99e4-cbb1a7d10a25" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573270 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -24\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -24 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ C & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -24\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -24 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\"." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573313 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186573158 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573313 #edb/ref 1069 "q-130869" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573313 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573313 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity m